{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover","id":803345,"title":"Demons and Hunters: The Lucifuge as a crossover?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-07T14:00:03-08:00","id":803345,"title":"Demons and Hunters: The Lucifuge as a crossover?","content":"I struck upon an interesting idea when I started looking into &quot;Heirs to Hell&quot;; could a member of the Lucifuge potentially have had a God-Machine Demon as a parent, rather than the traditional hell-fire and brimstone variety? Given how the Lucifuge have access to powers including the ability to understand all spoken languages, it'd make some sense. Or is there some kind of barrier with the Vigil that prevents the Unchained's children from joining?<br /> <br /> ...another interesting thought. The Hunter was a traditional Lucifuge, but then a Demon contracted one of their parents and subsumed that part of their history, changing their bloodline from one demon to another.<br /> <br /> For that matter, if a Demon manages to become a parent to one of the other supernaturals of the CoD universe, would it impact them in a way that prevents their being what they are? Would a Sin Eater who's father was replaced by the Unchained suddenly find themselves dead by way of their Geist not able to resurrect them, or would there just be something extra added in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":".  Mispelt Lucifuge 01-07-2016, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T14:13:11-08:00","id":803349,"title":"","content":"Mortal Remains details this crossover somewhat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T14:28:27-08:00","id":803358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=803349#post803349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortal Remains details this crossover somewhat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Darnit, and I've just gotten Hunter: The Vigil and various Demon products. XD I didn't need more to purchase!<br /> <br /> Still, that's a good resource to have, since I'm thinking of incorporating a Hunter into a Geist game I'm going to host.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T14:33:49-08:00","id":803360,"title":"","content":"Mortal Remains is the Hunter book that covers Promethean, Changeling, Geist, Mummy, and Demon. It's an absolute blast.<br /> <br /> Honestly, all the Hunter books are golden. I adore Night Stalkers, and Slasher is one if the best 1e books, to the point where the new edition is centered on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T09:03:49-08:00","id":803789,"title":"","content":"As to the more general question, there are two points to answer.<br /> <br /> 1. The Pact system only affects the party directly affected by the pact. So the child would not retroactively become a Demon-Blooded. (Of course, feel free to do so for the fun of it if you'd like).<br /> <br /> 2. As of 2e, there is precedent for Minor templates to remain when becoming a Major Template. I would say that a Demon-Blooded could still accept the Bargain and become a Bound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T14:27:52-08:00","id":804000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=803360#post803360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortal Remains is the Hunter book that covers Promethean, Changeling, Geist, Mummy, and Demon. It's an absolute blast.<br /> <br /> Honestly, all the Hunter books are golden. I adore Night Stalkers, and Slasher is one if the best 1e books, to the point where the new edition is centered on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bought Mortal Remains, and I agree it really does flesh out the various factions and how they view the different supernaturals. Good read, and it's definitely making me think of what I could do if Hunters were to emerge in one of my games...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=803789#post803789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the more general question, there are two points to answer.<br /> <br /> 1. The Pact system only affects the party directly affected by the pact. So the child would not retroactively become a Demon-Blooded. (Of course, feel free to do so for the fun of it if you'd like).<br /> <br /> 2. As of 2e, there is precedent for Minor templates to remain when becoming a Major Template. I would say that a Demon-Blooded could still accept the Bargain and become a Bound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for replying to those parts of my post. I was wondering because I'd read somewhere that, if a Demon takes the aspect of parenthood from someone (which happens if they become someone else as a cover), then their children have a chance of becoming Demonblood. It made me wonder if they took over a parent who had been related to an actual demon. Slim chance, of course, and it probably wouldn't overwrite a major template even if it did occur (so a member of the Lucifuge probably wouldn't suddenly not be a member on account of not being related to a relevant demon).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it'd be interesting if a child who became one of the Bound or Awakened suddenly found themselves awakening their Demonblood heritage...although that may simply complicate things considerably for the GM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T15:28:25-08:00","id":804061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=804000#post804000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, it'd be interesting if a child who became one of the Bound or Awakened suddenly found themselves awakening their Demonblood heritage...although that may simply complicate things considerably for the GM.</div> </div> </div> </div>You kidding? Provided they keep their Cypher, Free Sin-Eater/Mage!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T16:03:10-08:00","id":804083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=804061#post804061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You kidding? Provided they keep their Cypher, Free Sin-Eater/Mage!</div> </div> </div> </div>Cue the Mage finding himself by an Angelic &quot;Familiar&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T03:06:14-08:00","id":804310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=803789#post803789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the more general question, there are two points to answer.<br /> <br /> 1. The Pact system only affects the party directly affected by the pact. So the child would not retroactively become a Demon-Blooded. (Of course, feel free to do so for the fun of it if you'd like).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not true with demon children according to Heirs to Hell. If you take on the relationship between the parent and child (whether through soul pact or a specific patchwork), the child retroactively becomes an offspring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T10:15:24-08:00","id":807119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=804310#post804310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not true with demon children according to Heirs to Hell. If you take on the relationship between the parent and child (whether through soul pact or a specific patchwork), the child retroactively becomes an offspring.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, I must have missed that. Haven't actually run any Demon children yet. Thanks, that does add an interesting wrinkle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T12:55:49-08:00","id":807229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=804310#post804310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not true with demon children according to Heirs to Hell. If you take on the relationship between the parent and child (whether through soul pact or a specific patchwork), the child retroactively becomes an offspring.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=807119#post807119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I must have missed that. Haven't actually run any Demon children yet. Thanks, that does add an interesting wrinkle.</div> </div> </div> </div>That wrinkle makes me wonder what happens if a Lucifuge, who's demonic parentage is undone, suddenly finds themselves at odds with the conspiracy as a whole. On the one hand, they may or may not remember their time with the conspiracy (and if they do, do they keep any of the rituals that the Lucifuge call their own), but on the other, the leader of the group, the titular Lucifuge, isn't exactly human in her own right, and she may want to have a word with a member who's no longer a member.<br /> <br /> Whether it's a writing fumble or not, I really do like the ideas it brings up. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T13:07:33-08:00","id":807241,"title":"","content":"What's the issue? They'd likely still be able to have Castigations, I think, since Offspring are Stigmatic+, and Stigmatics are mostly human. And the Embeds they'd get by virtue of being Demon-Blooded are notably subtle in both execution and, for Offspring, possession. The write-up states that Offspring may not even consciously know they are doing anything particularly special.<br /> <hr /><br /> Huh. Now I'm wondering what is stopping a particularly &quot;generous&quot; Unchained from &quot;adopting&quot; large numbers of &quot;orphans&quot; to raise an army of Offspring...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-12-2016, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T15:50:56-08:00","id":807371,"title":"","content":"Probably the same issue as with most overt actions by demons - by virtue of becoming those childrens' parent, those children are suddenly related to one another, which could cause a bit of confusion about who went to bed with whom, and why the demon didn't stay with their new child longer. Likewise, more children means more mouths to feed and more attention to keep, especially if the unchained wants to make them particularly loyal and out of the God-Machine's sights. Offspring also don't have as many powers as their parents do, and while they can charge their embeds that usually makes things more apparent for the God-Machine to find.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T17:50:22-08:00","id":807464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=807241#post807241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the issue? They'd likely still be able to have Castigations, I think, since Offspring are Stigmatic+, and Stigmatics are mostly human.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. The child completely loses their heritage to Lucifer if you piecemeal pact with the parent who had the Lucifier blood rather than a soul pact, removing all their powers.<br /> 2. The child has a supernatural template, so they might not be able to the Hunter template. I mean, hell, they get Embeds, Glitches, and Interlocks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T18:58:36-08:00","id":807501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=807371#post807371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably the same issue as with most overt actions by demons - by virtue of becoming those childrens' parent, those children are suddenly related to one another, which could cause a bit of confusion about who went to bed with whom, and why the demon didn't stay with their new child longer. Likewise, more children means more mouths to feed and more attention to keep, especially if the unchained wants to make them particularly loyal and out of the God-Machine's sights. Offspring also don't have as many powers as their parents do, and while they can charge their embeds that usually makes things more apparent for the God-Machine to find.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't there a guy who had around 30 kids? And that's only one guy - buy 1 parentage, get 30 Offspring free. You can probably cut deals with others for them to raise the kids (it can happen now with foster homes, and that's for mere cash), or wait until they are &quot;ripe&quot; before making the above deal. Depending on how savvy you are, you should be able to rope a minion with Resources 5 to help maintain them, if needed. And as for power: they have more potential power than the average machine cultist. Embeds alone can be brutal, when employed correctly.<br /> <br /> (Note: Prospect Demon mega-parent doesn't <i>have</i> to be exploitive. They could just want more who might understand the Unchained plight, or genuinely take over dysfunctional or abusive parentages to help the kids.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=807464#post807464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. The child completely loses their heritage to Lucifer if you piecemeal pact with the parent who had the Lucifier blood rather than a soul pact, removing all their powers.<br /> 2. The child has a supernatural template, so they might not be able to the Hunter template. I mean, hell, they get Embeds, Glitches, and Interlocks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. Assuming they only got it from <i>one</i> side. Castigations don't require any qualifications other than being in the Lucifuge (Conspiracy). Sure, she <i>says</i> you've got the blood of hell in you. But maybe it's like having a royal in your ancestry - nearly everyone does nowadays, if you go back far enough.<br /> 2. Stigmatic isn't really a supernatural template (or much of one, at least). They can still pick up Supernatural Merits, which are limited to non-templated mortals. And Offspring are treated as stigmatics with a few extras.<br /> <br /> I could see it being argued either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-12-2016, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T21:00:39-08:00","id":807577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=807501#post807501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Assuming they only got it from <i>one</i> side. Castigations don't require any qualifications other than being in the Lucifuge (Conspiracy). Sure, she <i>says</i> you've got the blood of hell in you. But maybe it's like having a royal in your ancestry - nearly everyone does nowadays, if you go back far enough.<br /> 2. Stigmatic isn't really a supernatural template (or much of one, at least). They can still pick up Supernatural Merits, which are limited to non-templated mortals. And Offspring are treated as stigmatics with a few extras.<br /> <br /> I could see it being argued either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. As long as they only got it from one side yes. Which is more likely than not considering they are meant to be rare.<br /> 2. Stigmatic isn't the template they have. They have the Offspring template, which is abit more than just Stigmatic with a few extras. I mean for godsake they have a whole book dedicated to them, embeds, a cipher, interlocks, special systems like ambient aether, being able to store aether in their bodies, risk comprise, has instinctive knowledge of infrastructure, amazingly skilled with language and memory, they can sense when demons lie, have backtracing, exclusive conditions, etc. They both have stigmata and can see the gears, yes. But they're considerably more than just stigmatics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T21:19:04-08:00","id":807589,"title":"","content":"There's a couple things I like to keep in mind when dealing with broad concepts in ChroD, and for ease of memory I tend to associate little phrases with them; for instance, my shorthand for &quot;secondhand communication from [named higher power] can be dubious on both the origin-point and messenger fronts&quot; is &quot;Land of Ten Thousand Lunas.&quot;<br /> <br /> I mention this because my shorthand for &quot;supernatural categories are not necessarily of uniform ancestry and descent regardless of their gameline-compliant consistent mechanics&quot; happens to be &quot;The Lucifuge is the Lucifuge.&quot;<br /> <br /> Changing one bit of demonic ancestry for another doesn't make a member of the Seventh Generation less of an infernal scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T23:04:28-08:00","id":807634,"title":"","content":"I just assumed that the Lucifuge was effectively ejected from the conspiracy, due to their history not being compatable, but the leader of the Lucifuge remembers and takes the ejected member back into the fold as an &quot;unofficial consultant&quot;. The Lucifuge were always keeping tabs on the Unchained, so if they took in a member whom the leader remembered and could compare behaviors/memories to, well, wouldn't that be invaluable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T05:54:58-08:00","id":807805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=807589#post807589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changing one bit of demonic ancestry for another doesn't make a member of the Seventh Generation less of an infernal scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weirdly, Lucifuge's definition for what a &quot;demon&quot; is doesn't apply to Demons. Since there definition is a creature from other realm, but angels and demons are beings of the standard realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T14:32:46-08:00","id":813657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=803789#post803789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. As of 2e, there is precedent for Minor templates to remain when becoming a Major Template. I would say that a Demon-Blooded could still accept the Bargain and become a Bound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is this at? I have a Mage/Demon game I am in so I'm very interested in this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=804310#post804310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not true with demon children according to Heirs to Hell. If you take on the relationship between the parent and child (whether through soul pact or a specific patchwork), the child retroactively becomes an offspring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got a page number for this? <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T15:20:43-08:00","id":813687,"title":"","content":"Matt McFarland came in on the Heirs thread and said he was totally cool with wolf-blooded demon-blooded, demon-blooded Uratha, and demon-blooded Mages. That's where the former came from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T15:31:22-08:00","id":813695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=813687#post813687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Matt McFarland came in on the Heirs thread and said he was totally cool with wolf-blooded demon-blooded, demon-blooded Uratha, and demon-blooded Mages. That's where the former came from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think I could get a link to that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T17:56:20-08:00","id":813781,"title":"","content":"Wolf-Blooded don't stop being Wolf-Blooded either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T18:02:19-08:00","id":813783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=813657#post813657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Got a page number for this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pages 16-17 mention it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T18:12:44-08:00","id":813789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=813695#post813695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Think I could get a link to that?</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be a reference to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/174324-heirs-to-hell-questions?p=183244#post183244\">this</a> or <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/212169-being-a-wolf-blooded-fractal-your-opinion?p=222706#post222706\">this.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T18:20:21-08:00","id":813792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=813781#post813781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wolf-Blooded don't stop being Wolf-Blooded either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there isn't a big high fence around templates anymore.* In general, the question is &quot;can these things logically combine?&quot;<br /> <br /> In fact, thinking of a &quot;template&quot; as anything besides a character creation mechanism is misleading. And for hunters, specifically, we may or may not phrase that as a template in the new edition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*EDIT: In fact, if you look closely, we didn't really have one in old books either, although it was occasionally referred to.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T19:12:37-08:00","id":813825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=813792#post813792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, there isn't a big high fence around templates anymore.* In general, the question is &quot;can these things logically combine?&quot;<br /> <br /> In fact, thinking of a &quot;template&quot; as anything besides a character creation mechanism is misleading. And for hunters, specifically, we may or may not phrase that as a template in the new edition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*EDIT: In fact, if you look closely, we didn't really have one in old books either, although it was occasionally referred to.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I like template mixing, but then again I come from D&amp;D 3.5e where they have well over a hundred templates and all sorts of interesting things you can do with them.<br /> <br /> <br /> I will ask though, let's take the example of a Fractal Mage. Fractals use Cover and Mages use Wisdom. Which Integrity variant do they use, or do they use both?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Totally misread HtH.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 01-21-2016, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T19:16:13-08:00","id":813827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=813825#post813825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will ask though, let's take the example of a Fractal Mage. Fractals use Cover and Mages use Wisdom. Which Integrity variant do they use, or do they use both?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could do both if you wanted to. I'd swap over to Wisdom, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T19:17:00-08:00","id":813828,"title":"","content":"SNIP, Misread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 01-21-2016, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T19:18:58-08:00","id":813830,"title":"","content":"But I thought Fractals used Integrity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T19:19:28-08:00","id":813831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=813825#post813825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fractals use Cover</div> </div> </div> </div>No they don't. They use Integrity, like all Demon-Blooded. Heirs to Hell, page 34.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":".  Mistakenly said Flowers of Hell as the source book. 01-22-2016, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T19:23:03-08:00","id":813836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=813831#post813831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No they don't. They use Integrity, like all Demon-Blooded. Flowers of Hell, page 34.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, my mistake then. I must have misread HtH.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T02:33:50-08:00","id":814006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=813657#post813657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got a page number for this?</div> </div> </div> </div>17. Specifically it says &quot;One side-effect of these adoption pacts is that when the demon calls in the deal, the child becomes an Offspring&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T09:37:27-08:00","id":816944,"title":"","content":"I wonder, does this mean if you were a hunter and something changed that do you retain your endowments so long as you're not persona non grata?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T11:35:16-08:00","id":817021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=816944#post816944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder, does this mean if you were a hunter and something changed that do you retain your endowments so long as you're not persona non grata?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? As far as we know, nothing about many Hunter Endowments actually has much to restrict them, other than access. Advanced Armory just needs a RFID chip, Thaumatech only requires surgery, Elixers just have poison added, anyone can use Relics, and it seems like even Slashers retain access to Benedictions. About the only &quot;membership required&quot; Endowment is Castigations... and even those are questionable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T00:37:49-08:00","id":820811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803345-demons-and-hunters-the-lucifuge-as-a-crossover?p=817021#post817021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not? As far as we know, nothing about many Hunter Endowments actually has much to restrict them, other than access. Advanced Armory just needs a RFID chip, Thaumatech only requires surgery, Elixers just have poison added, anyone can use Relics, and it seems like even Slashers retain access to Benedictions. About the only &quot;membership required&quot; Endowment is Castigations... and even those are questionable.</div> </div> </div> </div> The hunter werewolf book talked about supernaturals having endowments, it came up with reasons (some of which contradict werewolf the forsaken by the by and a few others that didn't actually make sense) as to why werewolves can't have any of the major endowments but relics, so using that as an example an endowment would work for a supernatural unless there's a reason it wouldn't.<br /> <br /> For example, it said that werewolves can't use benedictions because benedictions requires a score in morality, morality equivalents don't cut it, so if one wanted to use that then benedictions would be a morality/integrity only option. <br /> <br /> Slashers discusses what happens when a psychic actually joins Vanguard (psychics being a template in first edition, probably replaced by supernatural merits in second edition), it says that psychics can keep psychic powers and gain access to teleinformics if the ST is okay with it, and Compacts and Conspiracies mentions that Chiron bribes some vampires and witches with thaumatech implants, and that some AO are trying to build their own prometheans as new members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T02:57:47-08:00","id":820856,"title":"","content":"Can I say I love the discussion this is bringing up?<br /> <br /> I think, in general, gear that Hunters have <i>can</i> make its way into most hands provided there is some kind of logical reasoning for it. Sin Eaters may get their hands on some of Project: VALKYRIE's ghost-hurting bullets if the mail goes to the wrong address, or relics may get into the hands of some random person if they find it first. Likewise, the gamebook describes a janitor accidentally being inducted into the Hunters and filled with thaumatech as a case of mistaken identity, so some random person being kitted with Hunter gear without a personal connection to the Vigil may get it. It just needs to be a massive coincidence, and probably isn't repeatable.<br /> <br /> The same can't be said for the general gear in the Hunter book though - I was seriously surprised when I found laptops, cellphones and various other normal gear in the Hunter book and not the core book. Seems like a bit of an afterthought...though that is going off topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}